claim.claim-text:
identifying, based on the first join keys and second join keys corresponding to conversions for which the multiple client devices provided conversion data to the second aggregation server, groups of encrypted conversion data and corresponding encrypted impression data;
ordering, for each chronological sequence, the encrypted conversion data and the corresponding encrypted impression data based on the encrypted impression time data and encrypted conversion time data corresponding to each second join key; and
decrypting the impression data and the conversion data for each sequence of encrypted impression data and conversion data in multiple stages using a first private key that corresponds to the first public key and a second private key that corresponds to the second public key.

decrypting, by the first aggregation server, each encrypted conversion time data;
determining, by the first aggregation server, for each unique encrypted conversion data, a number of unique second join keys;
filtering, from a set of encrypted conversion data received by the first aggregation server, each encrypted conversion data for which the number of unique second join keys is less than a threshold; and
providing, for each remaining encrypted conversion data in the set of encrypted conversion data, a tuple of data that includes the second join key for the encrypted conversion data and the encrypted conversion data.

decrypt each encrypted impression time data;
determining, for each unique encrypted conversion data, a number of unique first join keys;
filter, from a set of encrypted impression data received by the second aggregation server, each encrypted impression data for which the number of unique first join keys is less than a threshold; and
provide, for each remaining encrypted conversion data in the set of encrypted impression data, a tuple of data that includes the first join key for the encrypted impression data and the encrypted conversion data.
